e this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $80,$ and the percentage is $115\\%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n115\\%=115÷100=1.15\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =115\\%\\times 80 \\\\  & =1.15\\times 80 \\\\  & =92\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $115\\%$ of $80$ is $92.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n115\\%=\\frac{115}{100}=\\frac{115÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{23}{20}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =115\\%\\times 80 \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{20}\\times 80 \\\\  & =23\\times \\frac{80}{20} \\\\  & =23\\times 4 \\\\  & =92\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $115\\%$ of $80$ is $92.$"] [:db/cas 17592186441685 :question/problem "$16%$ of $75$ is equal to{{field-1}}." "$16\\%$ of $75$ is equal to{{field-1}}."] [:db/cas 17592186441685 :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $75,$ and the percentage is $16%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n16%=16÷100=0.16\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =16%\\times 75 \\\\  & =0.16\\times 75 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $16%$ of $75$ is $12.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n16%=\\frac{16}{100}=\\frac{16÷4}{100÷4}=\\frac{4}{25}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =16%\\times 75 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{25}\\times 75 \\\\  & =4\\times \\frac{75}{25} \\\\  & =4\\times 3 \\\\  & =12\\e