emotely?"] [:db/cas 17592186486403 :question/worked-solution "Let $x$ be the number of employees last year.\n\nWe're told that the total number increased to $125%$ of last year’s total. Thus, the current number of employees is $1.25x.$\n\nWe are also told that of these employees, $20%$ work remotely. So, the number of employees working remotely is\n\n$$\n0.20(1.25x)=0.25x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.25x$ represents $25%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $25%$ of last year’s employees now work remotely." "Let $x$ be the number of employees last year.\n\nWe're told that the total number increased to $125\\%$ of last year’s total. Thus, the current number of employees is $1.25x.$\n\nWe are also told that of these employees, $20\\%$ work remotely. So, the number of employees working remotely is\n\n$$\n0.20(1.25x)=0.25x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.25x$ represents $25\\%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $25\\%$ of last year’s employees now work remotely."] [:db/cas 17592186486404 :question/problem "A museum’s attendance decreased to $80%$ of its previous level. Then, a promotion increased attendance by $25%.$ If the museum originally had $24,000$ attendees, how many attendees were added by the promotion?\n\nThe number of attendees added is  \n{{field-1}}." "A museum’s attendance decreased to $80\\%$ of its previous level. Then, a promotion increased attendance by $25\\%.$ If the museum originally had $24,000$ attendees, how many attendees were added by the promotion?\n\nThe number of attendees added is  \n{{field-1}}."] [:db/cas 17592186486404 :question/worked-solution "First, the new attendance is $80%$ of the previous level $(24,000$ attendees$):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}80%\\times 24,000 & =\\frac{80}{100}\\times 24,000 \\\\  & =0.8\\times 24,000 \\\\  & =19,200\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the new attendance is $19,200.$ Then, the attendees added by the promotion is $25%$ of this new attendance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25%\\times 19,200 & =\\frac{25}{100}\\times 19,200 \\\\  & =0.25\\times 19,200 \\\\  &