e account?"] [:db/cas 17592186486426 :question/worked-solution "In our situation:\n\n- During the day, the account had a *deposit of* $$20,$ which is a change of $+$20.$\n\n- Later, the account had a *withdrawal of* $$20,$ which is a change of $-$20.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0:$\n\n$$\n20+(-20)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the balance returns to its original value of $$0.$" "In our situation:\n\n- During the day, the account had a *deposit of* $\\$20,$ which is a change of $+$20.$\n\n- Later, the account had a *withdrawal of* $$20,$ which is a change of $-\\$20.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0:$\n\n$$\n20+(-20)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the balance returns to its original value of $\\$0.$"] [:db/cas 17592186486434 :question/problem "Find $30%$ of $50,$ and then $20%$ of the result." "Find $30\\%$ of $50,$ and then $20\\%$ of the result."] [:db/cas 17592186486434 :question/worked-solution "First, we find $30%$ of $50:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30%\\times 50 & =\\frac{30}{100}\\times 50 \\\\  & =0.3\\times 50 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find $20%$ of the result $(15):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20%\\times 15 & =\\frac{20}{100}\\times 15 \\\\  & =0.2\\times 15 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $3.$" "First, we find $30\\%$ of $50:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30\\%\\times 50 & =\\frac{30}{100}\\times 50 \\\\  & =0.3\\times 50 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find $20\\%$ of the result $(15):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20\\%\\times 15 & =\\frac{20}{100}\\times 15 \\\\  & =0.2\\times 15 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $3.$"] [:db/cas 17592186486435 :question/problem "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n=66$ from a population where $42%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th